    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1038">

                <pb facs="0779" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/4212.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister at Mexico
                            City to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 10, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Silliman is still at Saltillo under arrest. Marchani, his clerk, left this
                    morning for Vera Cruz. Other Americans from Saltillo leave to-morrow morning for
                    Vera Cruz. They all confirm circumstances attending removal of archives, money,
                    valuables, code, from Consulate by Mexican officials. Have made strongest
                    representations concerning release of Silliman and the restoration of code and
                    other property of the United States. Have asked that Silliman be delivered to me
                    and that he should be allowed to leave country under full protection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
